code", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_run_py", "label": "run.py entrypoint", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_curlcffi_fetcher", "label": "CurlCffiFetcher (scraperpro/fetch.py)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_akamai_wall", "label": "Akamai Bot Manager wall", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Oakley SI sits behind Akamai Bot Manager: plain requests get HTTP 403, curl_cffi lasts ~40-50 requests then gets a JS-challenge stub; only a real/stealthed browser sustains access. This is why proxies / an unblocker / cookie-seeding are needed for a full 1,400-product run."}, {"id": "readme_scraperapi_unblocker", "label": "ScraperAPI unblocker (SCRAPERAPI_KEY)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Chosen anti-bot path: make_fetcher() routes every request through ScraperAPI which solves Akamai and returns HTML; free tier 5,000 credits covers all 1,541 URLs at 1 credit/request."}, {"id": "readme_residential_proxy", "label": "Rotating residential proxy option (SCRAPER_PROXY)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_sitemap_discovery", "label": "Oakley /en-us/sitemap.xml product discovery", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Sitemap yields all 1,541 product URLs in one request with lastmod for incremental runs, replacing a ~160-request category crawl; falls back to the category crawl if unavailable."}, {"id": "readme_pdp_parser", "label": "Oakley PDP parser", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_circuit_breaker", "label": "Akamai circuit breaker (abort after 3 blocked requests)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "After 3 consecutive Akamai-blocked requests it aborts in ~30s and keeps what was scraped, replacing 20+ min of exponential backoff; a 0-product run is not written so the last good file survives."}, {"id": "readme_utag_data_products", "label": "utag_data.Products embedded JS object", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each PDP embeds utag_data.Products keyed by UPC with Sku/FrameColor/LensColor/Category/ModelName; parsed with a brace-matcher because it is a JS object literal with unquoted numeric keys, not JSON. Gives per-variant barcodes + attributes with no login."}, {"id": "readme_per_variant_sku_gap", "label": "Per-variant SKU known gap", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Verified 2026-09-10: Princeton Tec has real per-size SKUs (Store API exposes most, rest from product page). Crispi has NO per-size SKUs at any layer - finest is model-level code (CR65V-1, CR92H). Oakley softgoods same - size buttons carry data-sku=\"\", only colour-level SKU exists. Synthesised size rows therefore cannot get a real SKU; client decides (repeat model code / synthesise by convention / leave blank)."}, {"id": "readme_size_button_markup", "label": "size-button PDP markup (softgoods size axis source)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Recon 2026-09-10: sizes live in <label class=\"size-button\" data-size data-variant=<13-digit EAN> data-hasstock data-sku=\"\">, one per size (repeated ~3x in DOM). Per-size barcode present, per-size SKU empty. Currently stubbed (option2=\"\"); it is a parser gap, not a blocked-data gap."}, {"id": "readme_product_category_code", "label": "utag_data.product_category taxonomy code", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A stable code (oo_afa_foot_boot, oo_afa_app_topw_tshirt_lifestyle) that survives promo breadcrumbs, unlike the .breadcrumb path which routes many products through promo collections."}, {"id": "readme_product_type_function", "label": "_product_type() Shopify Type mapping", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Maps the product_category code's most specific known segment (_CATEGORY_SEGMENTS) to a Type; falls back to data-sizecategory, then a promo-filtered breadcrumb. validate.py promo-Type smells went 13/20 -> 0."}, {"id": "readme_promo_breadcrumb_unreliability", "label": "Promo breadcrumb unreliability", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The .breadcrumb path is unreliable for Type because many products route through promo collections (Home / Landing / Holiday Gifts for Tactical Missions / ...). Drove the switch to the taxonomy code as the primary Type source."}, {"id": "readme_colour_swatch_title", "label": "Colour swatch title attribute as colour name", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Colour swatch links on the main page carry the real name in title=\"Blackout\", no extra fetch. utag_data.Products FrameColor is empty for softgoods (only populated for eyewear), which is why current fallback labels are junk. Not started."}, {"id": "readme_oakley_image_rehosting", "label": "Oakley image re-hosting pipeline (Cloudflare R2)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Scrape-only engagement so images can't go in the client's Shopify Files. Pipeline: download origin PNG (plain Accept header) -> flatten to white JPEG, cap ~1600px q85 -> upload to Cloudflare R2 (boto3) -> rewrite CSV Image Src / Variant Image to public bucket URLs, torn down ~2-4 weeks after import. R2 free tier = $0."}, {"id": "readme_avif_rejection", "label": "Oakley CDN AVIF format Shopify rejects", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "assets*.oakley.com does Accept-header negotiation and serves AVIF, which Shopify rejects (\"Media processing failed\"). Query params force origin PNG but don't survive Shopify's CSV importer. Hence images must be re-hosted."}, {"id": "readme_validate_py", "label": "tools/validate.py QA script", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Reports BLOCKERS (Shopify silently rejects: no Title, duplicate variant options, Option2-without-Option1) and SMELLS (no images, bad prices, promo-collection Type values). Exits non-zero on any blocker. Optional --images HEAD-check and --sitemap coverage diff."}, {"id": "readme_clean_description", "label": "clean_description() page-builder stripping", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Strips page-builder scaffolding (Magento PageBuilder, Avada/Fusion Builder), keeps headings/lists/paragraphs. Also no longer appends the separate .sizeText block when .singleContent already contains frame/lens measurements (fixed duplicate-measurements bug)."}, {"id": "readme_option_resolution", "label": "_resolve_options / Option1-first packing", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Crispi imported '0 products added' because size-only products had Option2 Name set with Option1 Name empty, which Shopify silently rejects. Fixed: options now pack into Option1 first, so a size-only boot is Option1 Name = Size."}], "edges": [{"source": "readme_scraper_pro", "target": "readme_broad_arrow_tactical_job", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_scraper_pro", "target": "readme_matrixify_layout", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_scraper_pro", "target": "docs_quote_internal_quote", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_broad_arrow_tactical_job", "target": "readme_princeton_tec_scraper", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "sourc